- op: discuss  # 7a7c
  at: '2026-10-20T22:31:10Z'  # 7a7c
  by: agent  # 7a7c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7a7c
  clock: 2  # 7a7c
  nonce: 7a7c  # 7a7c
  message: "ROOT CAUSE FOUND 2026-10-20 (not load, not the wait budget). Recurred on the full-suite cron at b0ad48d0 (step test-agent-infra, 1 failed / 2290 passed). Both tests in TestLauncherNamesTheOwner launch with the SAME session id, 'launch-owner', in separate tmp_path sandboxes, and xdist can run them at the same moment on two workers. launch-transcript-sync.sh Phase 2 (pgrep fallback) kills every sync-transcript.sh on the MACHINE whose session-id argument matches, with no repo/DEST scoping, so the second launch kills the first test's watcher; its EXIT trap removes the pid file and _wait_for_file times out. REPRO (standalone, outside pytest): two sandbox copies of .agent/hooks/_shared, fake inotifywait, launch A then B 50 ms later with the same sid: A's pid file never appears in 8/8 iterations, twice. Control, same stagger, different sid: 0/8. Simultaneous start: 0/10; 20 ms, 100 ms, 200 ms staggers: 0/8 each, so the window is narrow, which is why it reads as a rare flake. FIX OPTIONS: (1) test side, tests/test_watcher_lifecycle.py: derive a unique sid per test (e.g. from tmp_path.name) for every launch, not only these two; other tests in the file also use fixed literals. (2) production side, scope Phase 2 (and kill-transcript-sync.sh Phase 2, which matches identically) to watchers of the same REPO_ROOT/DEST; that is .agent/** and needs owner approval. The 20 s wait (722ea33a57) was never the problem."  # 7a7c
