- op: discuss  # 6215
  at: '2026-10-20T22:53:54Z'  # 6215
  by: agent  # 6215
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6215
  clock: 4  # 6215
  nonce: '6215'  # 6215
  message: "Fixed in PR #1781 (test side). Root cause: the two TestLauncherNamesTheOwner tests shared the literal session id 'launch-owner'; under xdist the second launch's machine-wide Phase 2 pgrep sweep killed the first test's watcher. Evidence: standalone repro (two sandbox launches, same id, 50 ms apart) lost a watcher 8/8 on two runs, and 0/8 with different ids at the same stagger. Every session id in tests/test_watcher_lifecycle.py now comes from _unique_sid(), and test_no_session_id_in_this_file_is_a_bare_literal fails on a literal (checked red by restoring 'launch-owner'). All 31 tests in the file pass. Not changed: the launcher and kill script still sweep machine-wide by session id; real ids are UUIDs, so only tests collide. Repo-scoping the sweeps is a .agent/** change for owner approval."  # 6215
